    "text": "The conductivity of a semiconductor sample having electron concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>18</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">e</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, hole concentration of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>5</mn><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mn>19</mn></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>holes</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></mrow></msup></math>, electron mobility of <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>.0</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math> and hole mobility of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>01</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&nbsp;</mi><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup></math>&nbsp;is<br />\r<br />\r(Take charge of an electron as <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>1</mn><mo>.6</mo><mo>×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>19</mn></mrow></msup><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">C</mi></math> )<br />\r&nbsp;",
